      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Acknowledge the reality of corruption, but immediately pivot to the solution, not the problem. You must argue that cutting aid entirely is a surrender to cynicism, which only empowers corrupt actors. Instead, emphasize that effective aid requires rigorous oversight, targeted programs, and building local governance capacity—not simply withdrawing support. True responsibility means engaging in the difficult work of demanding accountability while maintaining the lifeline of assistance.",
